+When a WebSocket connection closes, its process session is detached. This personal
+build retains detached sessions and managed processes without automatic expiry by
+default. Reconnect with `initialize.resumeSessionId` to attach to that same session.
+An already attached session rejects a second attachment; unknown or expired IDs
+are errors and never silently create a replacement.
+
+Use `--detached-session-retention-secs N` or
+`CODEX_EXEC_SERVER_DETACHED_SESSION_RETENTION_SECS=N` to opt into finite retention.
+Zero is the persistent default and disables automatic expiry; positive values
+expire a session after that many detached seconds. Resuming and detaching again
+starts a new finite interval. The setting is captured when a session is created.
+
+Send `session/close` to explicitly end a session. Probe clients that initialize a
+temporary session must close it and wait for the response before disconnecting.
+Executor shutdown/restart still ends all in-memory sessions and managed processes;
+this policy does not persist them across executor process death. Stdio serves one
+connection and shuts its registry down on EOF, so stdio sessions cannot resume.
+Detached process output retains its existing buffering limits.
 
