+### `session/close` (personal executor extension)
+
+After `initialize` and `initialized`, send a request with `{}` params:
+
+```json
+{"id": 9, "method": "session/close", "params": {}}
+```
+
+The response is `{"id":9,"result":{}}`. It removes only the session attached to
+that connection, terminates its managed processes and closes its connection-local
+resources. It accepts no target session ID and cannot close another connection's
+session. Concurrent queued/in-flight RPC work is canceled before closing. After
+the response, disconnect; the session ID is terminal and cannot be resumed.
+
+This method is additive: the existing initialize wire shape is unchanged. Older
+executors return JSON-RPC `-32601`; clients must report unsupported cleanup rather
+than claim the session was closed. A missing response has an unknown outcome and
+must not cause command replay or a new session.
+
 Params are currently ignored. Sending any other notification method is treated
 as an invalid request.
 
